From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LNPANDY <lnp-andy@hotmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 18:43:24 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Mac: split a Joy-Con pair into two sideways controllers
 (#740)

When DM_JOYCON_SPLIT=1 is set on macOS, front_mac.m skips GameController's combined Joy-Con input and reads Joy-Con (L) (0x057e:0x2006) and Joy-Con (R) (0x057e:0x2007) directly over IOHIDManager 0x30 reports so each half gets its own player slot with a 90-degree sideways stick and 6-axis IMU rotation, SL/SR mapped to L/R, and per-handle Core Haptics rumble (GCHapticsLocalityLeftHandle and GCHapticsLocalityRightHandle).

Upstream-Status: forwarded seedds/nxnative#1322
Reason: Mac: split a Joy-Con pair into two sideways controllers over HID 0x30 with motion and rumble
Issue: LNPANDY/NX2Apple#740
